    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float x;\n    float y;\n} Point;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n    float *xs;\n    float *ys;\n} Group;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float dist;\n    char label;\n} KNNEntry;\n\nvoid on_error() {\n    printf(\"Invalid input file.\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\" n_groups=%d \", &n) != 1) on_error();\n    return n;\n}\n\nPoint parse_point() {\n    float x, y;\n    if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\n    Point point;\n    point.x = x;\n    point.y = y;\n    return point;\n}\n\nGroup parse_next_group() {\n    char label; \n    int length;\n    if (scanf(\" label=%c \", &label) != 1) on_error();\n    if (scanf(\" length=%d \", &length) != 1) on_error();\n\n    Group group;\n    group.label = label;\n    group.length = length;\n    group.xs = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * length);\n    group.ys = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * length);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        float x, y;\n        if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2) on_error();\n        group.xs[i] = x;\n        group.ys[i] = y;\n    }\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nint parse_k() {\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\" k=%d \", &k) != 1) on_error();\n    return k;\n}\n\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\n    float dx = b.x - a.x;\n    float dy = b.y - a.y;\n    return dx * dx + dy * dy;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.h"
    },
    {
      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    KNNEntry *entries = (KNNEntry *) malloc(sizeof(KNNEntry) * k);\n    if (!entries) exit(1);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        entries[i].dist = -1.0f;\n        entries[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    int filled = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        float *xs = g.xs;\n        float *ys = g.ys;\n        char label = g.label;\n        int len = g.length;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, \n                (Point){xs[j], ys[j]});\n\n            // Binary search insertion point among first filled entries\n            int lo = 0, hi = filled;\n            while (lo < hi) {\n                int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                if (entries[mid].dist <= d)\n                    lo = mid + 1;\n                else\n                    hi = mid;\n            }\n            int pos = lo; // first index where dist > d, or filled if all <=\n\n            if (filled < k) {\n                memmove(&entries[pos+1], &entries[pos], sizeof(KNNEntry)*(filled - pos));\n                entries[pos].dist = d;\n                entries[pos].label = label;\n                filled++;\n            } else if (pos < k) { // full and new distance is smaller than some existing\n                memmove(&entries[pos+1], &entries[pos], sizeof(KNNEntry)*(k - pos - 1));\n                entries[pos].dist = d;\n                entries[pos].label = label;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Frequency counting using histogram (max 256 possible labels)\n    int freq[256] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < filled; i++) {\n        unsigned char uc = (unsigned char)entries[i].label;\n        freq[uc]++;\n    }\n\n    char most_frequent = -1;\n    int max_count = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 256; i++) {\n        if (freq[i] > max_count) {\n            max_count = freq[i];\n            most_frequent = (char)i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(entries);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Changing data layout from Array-of-Structs (Point) to Struct-of-Arrays (separate xs and ys arrays per group) improves cache line utilization when computing distances by enabling sequential streaming of coordinates, which can be prefetched efficiently. Using an array-of-structs for the k-nearest neighbors list reduces memory traffic during insertion shifts because all fields are contiguous in memory. Replacing linear scan with binary search + memmove reduces comparisons and data movement. Replacing qsort+scan frequency counting with a direct histogram eliminates sorting overhead entirely.",
  "notes": "This experiment combines data layout changes at both group level (SoA for coordinates) and top-k list level (AoS for distance+label), along with algorithmic improvements to insertion (binary search + memmove) and final classification (histogram instead of sort).",
